  "body": "## Goal\nMake seller-response handling configurable per negotiation step instead of always escalating immediately.\n\n## Per-step behavior\nEach step now configures:\n- what to do after a formal Vinted rejection: send next step immediately or wait N hours\n- fallback behavior for a seller counteroffer\n- any number of counteroffer discount thresholds, where discount is ALWAYS measured from the original listing price\n- highest matching percentage threshold wins\n\nExample defaults migrated to existing bots:\n- step 1 rejection -> next step immediately\n- step 2 rejection -> wait 6h\n- step 3 rejection -> wait 12h\n- step 4+ rejection -> wait 24h\n- seller counteroffer below 10% discount -> wait 6h\n- seller counteroffer >=10% discount -> wait 2h\n- seller counteroffer >=15% discount -> next step immediately\n\n## Important mechanics\n- existing `maxAcceptedCounterOffer` remains highest-priority: a seller price within that threshold goes to ACTION_REQUIRED immediately\n- if the seller's price is already at/below our planned next offer, it also goes to ACTION_REQUIRED instead of irrationally offering more than the seller asked\n- formal rejection/counteroffer first-detection timestamps are persisted in the backend so 6h/12h/24h timers do not restart on every poll\n- a changed seller counteroffer creates a new fingerprint/timer\n- new negotiation step resets the old response timer\n- delayed rules fail closed if the response timestamp cannot be persisted\n- pending/read/normal-message 3h policy remains separate and unchanged\n- adaptive pricing/global cap/quota/idempotency/real-action guards remain intact\n\n## Existing bots\nFlyway V25 migrates all existing step policies and adds the default 10%/15% rules. Existing negotiations are preserved; no destructive reset is needed.\n\nResponse/timing policy fields are safe to edit while active negotiations exist. Prices, accepted-counter thresholds, messages and step structure remain locked while active.\n\n## UI\nThe bot create/edit step cards now contain a dedicated response-policy editor with:\n- rejection action + optional wait time\n- counteroffer fallback action\n- add/remove percentage rules\n- per-rule action and wait time\n- explicit explanation that percentages are measured from original listing price\n- mobile-responsive styling\n\n## Tests\nAdds deterministic Playwright coverage for immediate/delayed rejection, 10%/15% seller concessions, original-price percentage calculation, stable response fingerprints and the never-offer-more-than-seller guard.",
